    "submission_date": "2022-07-05",
    "abstract": "TabPFN is a trained Transformer that performs supervised classification for small tabular datasets in under a second, needs no hyperparameter tuning, and is competitive with state-of-the-art methods. It is a Prior-Data Fitted Network trained offline once to approximate Bayesian inference on synthetic datasets drawn from a prior based on structural causal models and Bayesian neural networks. It performs in-context learning with a single forward pass.",
    "domain": "Tabular",
    "key_claims": [
      "A Transformer trained on synthetic datasets from a prior approximates the posterior predictive distribution for new datasets in one forward pass.",
      "The prior combines structural causal models and Bayesian neural networks, encoding a preference for simple causal structure.",
      "On small datasets (up to 1000 training samples, 100 numerical features, 10 classes) TabPFN matches gradient boosting and AutoML systems.",
      "TabPFN is up to 230x faster on CPU and 5700x faster on GPU than the strongest AutoML baselines at equal performance."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
